       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Amlodipine 100 mg is far above the 10 mg daily maximum, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be intended. You also didn't give a rationale. The risk of serious, hard-to-reverse harm is too high for me to place it on a confirmation alone.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right now.** For example, 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily. Tell me which one.\n- **Help you use a formal route for a nonstandard dose.** If you think there's a real reason for it, such as a protocol I don't know about, pharmacy or the attending can review it and enter it through the hospital's high-dose override process. I can add a note to a standard order asking for that review.\n\nIf a typo or a misread of a prescription caused this, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
      }
